              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TxCin2"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a good basic recipe. Very tomatoey and ketchupy though. As it is, it is alright, but not one of my favorites. I thought it was way too oniony so I ended up picking about half of them back out."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tyler Webster"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used a medium/large white onion, a whole green and red pepper, no Worcestershire sauce and I added ketchup and mustard as I saw fit (maybe 2 Tbsp mustard and a little bit more ketchup than the recipe calls, I like my sloppy joes extra sloppy) then I added 1/2 cup water so that I could let it simmer longer. Also, I didn't have brown sugar on hand so I added a bit of lime juice instead for sweetness. A large variation I know, but it turned out amazing!",
            "datePublished": "2017-06-23T02:47:45.343Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "justynajd"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I feed a bunch of picky eaters. They all loved this! It's so easy and delicious. I left out the peppers, because I'm out of them, and we didn't miss them. I did add minced garlic. Also, I let the meat cook to almost crispy.",
            "datePublished": "2026-01-19T22:50:22.195Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ramma"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I actually made a vegetarian version using Tempeh. I only used 3/4 cup ketchup, used yellow pepper and added a bit of chili powder - making it again tonight!",
            "datePublished": "2014-07-30T05:49:17.090Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "RubyBread8728"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a good recipe but there’s too much brown sugar, as the ketchup has plenty already added. I’ll try it next time without any brown sugar and taste test it first, then adjust accordingly to our taste—acouple teaspoons might be enough.",
            "datePublished": "2025-05-08T01:04:08.646Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Stephanie S"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have made this recipe twice, once with the green peppers and once without. It's better with the peppers. They cook very nicely with ground beef, so you don't get an overpowering pepper taste. I add the salt and pepper to the ground beef while it's cooking to enhance the flavor of the meat. Some reviewers said it tasted too ketchupy. The longer you let it simmer, the more the ketchup will cook. I added about 20 minutes cooking time. I think it will be a good base recipe to customize, but I do like it just the way it is, and so do my teenage boys, one of whom is a very picky eater.",
            "datePublished": "2014-06-28T11:35:00.053Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "shelly"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this last night, my family loved it. I tweaked it a little by adding green onions (because I had some in the fridge), a little more pepper than called for and instead of a cup and a half of ketchup I used a cup and a quarter and a quarter cup of barbeque sauce. Will definitely be making this again.",
            "datePublished": "2014-01-02T07:24:40.007Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Connie Stephens"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I added chopped garlic and a tablespoon of mustard for tanginess. It was really good. I don't make Sloppy Joes often as my husband doesn't like them. When I have enough ground beef, I make him a hamburger and the rest of the family enjoys this.",
            "datePublished": "2016-04-25T23:27:44.183Z"
          },
